A **Code 1** learner's licence authorises riding a **motorcycle** (but not a motor quadrucycle) on a public road.
(i) Minimum age is **16**;
(ii) under 18 you're limited to a **125cc** engine;
(iii) **no passengers** may be carried.

A **Code 2** learner's licence authorises driving any motor vehicle or combination (other than a motorcycle or tricycle) with tare, GVM, or GCM **not exceeding 3500kg**, only under the **direct supervision** of a licensed driver for that class.
(i) Minimum age is **17**;
(ii) valid for **24 months** from the test date.

A **Code 3** learner's licence authorises driving any motor vehicle or combination (other than a motorcycle, tricycle, or quadrucycle) -- covering both light and heavy vehicles -- only under the **direct supervision** of a licensed driver for that class.
(i) Minimum age is **18**;
(ii) valid for **24 months** from the test date.
